{
 "description": "Contract cases for the category list, version 3 (INT-010, ADR-0060, AC 1, 13, 32, 33, 34). One file shared by category_policy, the agent and the api. 'normalise' rows give the expected comparison key of a name; 'label' rows the Gmail label of a name, which is the canonical list name without any prefix. 'category' rows validate one category: 'existing' are the names already on the list, 'labels' the Gmail labels that exist (the caller's view) and 'adoptable' the subset of them that belongs to an older category, which a new category of the same name adopts instead of clashing; 'rules' is the exact list of refusal rule ids in reporting order, empty means valid. A name of the form __label_len_N__ stands for a valid nested name of N characters (segments of 40 letters); the limit counts Unicode characters, not bytes, slashes included. A description of the form __N__ stands for N letters. 'list' rows validate a whole list; 'problems' is a list of [index, rule] pairs, index null for a rule about the whole list; 'generate' N stands for N valid categories. 'instructions' rows give the length of the general instructions (N letters) and the exact refusal rule ids. 'label_setting' rows validate the name of the Other label or the archive label: 'counterpart' is the current name of the other setting, 'categories' the list names, 'rules' the exact refusal rule ids (at most one); a row with 'repeat' stands for 'fill' repeated that many times instead of 'name'. 'bounds' rows validate one agent setting by 'setting' (wait_minutes 5 to 720, protection_days 1 to 30, retention_days 7 to 90) with a whole number 'value'. Invisible characters and look-alikes use unicode escapes.",
